---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const contact = (await getEntry("contact", "contact"))!.data;
const email = contact.enquiry_email || contact.email;
const updated = "19 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="When and how you get your money back on a GrintByte product."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Refund policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-grint mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">The short version</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If a product does not work as described on its product page and we cannot fix it for you,
          you get a full refund. Ask within 14 days of your purchase.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">How to ask</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="text-brand underline">{email}</a> with the email
          address you used at checkout, the product name and a short description of the problem.
          Most issues turn out to be quick fixes, so we will first try to solve it with you. If we
          cannot get the product working as described, we refund the full purchase price, no
          further questions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">What is covered</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>The product does not do what its product page says, and support cannot resolve it.</li>
          <li>The product cannot be installed or activated in an environment it claims to support.</li>
          <li>You were charged twice, or charged for something you did not order.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We cannot offer a refund when a product works as described but you changed your mind, or
          when a request arrives later than 14 days after the purchase. If you think your case is
          an exception, email us anyway; we read every request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">How the money comes back</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Refunds are issued by our payment provider to the payment method you used at checkout.
          We trigger the refund as soon as we approve it; depending on your bank or card issuer, it
          usually appears within 5 to 10 business days.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
